# .understandignore — patterns for files/dirs to exclude from analysis
# Syntax: same as .gitignore (globs, # comments, ! negation, trailing / for dirs)
#
# SCOPE: core + transports, tests INCLUDED.
#   packages/core/src, packages/shared/src,
#   apps/{tools-api,mcp-client,web-ui,opencode-plugin}/src
#
# Tests live inside those src/ trees (core/src/__tests__, tools-api routes'
# sibling *.test.ts, web-ui/src/__tests__) and are deliberately kept so the
# graph carries tested_by edges and "tested" node tags.
#
# NOTE: gitignore semantics cannot re-include a file under an excluded parent,
# so out-of-scope paths are listed explicitly rather than via allowlist+negation.

# --- Generated byte-identical duplicates of skills/ (652 files) ---
# scripts/generate-skill-artifacts.ts emits these; analyzing them would create
# 4x duplicate nodes for every real skill file. See CLAUDE.md "Agent-harness surface".
apps/claude-plugin/
apps/codex-plugin/
apps/cursor-plugin/
apps/opencode-plugin/skills/
apps/opencode-plugin/agents/
apps/opencode-plugin/lib/

# --- Out of scope: harness sources, specs, benchmarks, build/release machinery ---
